# Project Structure Guide

This is a **react-node-utils** monorepo containing utility packages for different environments and use cases.

## Package Overview

### 🌐 Universal Utilities
- **[packages/universal](mdc:packages/universal)** - Platform-agnostic utilities that work in any JavaScript environment
- **[packages/types](mdc:packages/types)** - Shared TypeScript type definitions and Zod playground

### 🖥️ Environment-Specific Utilities  
- **[packages/browser](mdc:packages/browser)** - Browser-only utilities (array, regex, sizeof, string manipulation)
- **[packages/node](mdc:packages/node)** - Node.js utilities (CLI tools, JWT handling)

### ⚛️ React/Next.js Utilities
- **[packages/next-react](mdc:packages/next-react)** - React components and Next.js utilities with Storybook documentation

### 📚 Documentation
- **[packages/docs](mdc:packages/docs)** - Project documentation and guides

## Development Setup

The project uses [pnpm](mdc:pnpm-workspace.yaml) workspaces with the following key commands:

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Build all packages
pnpm build

# Run tests across all packages  
pnpm test

# Lint and format
pnpm lint
pnpm prettier
```

## Configuration Files

- **[package.json](mdc:package.json)** - Root package configuration
- **[tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json)** - TypeScript configuration
- **[vitest.workspace.ts](mdc:vitest.workspace.ts)** - Test configuration
- **[.eslintrc.cjs](mdc:.eslintrc.cjs)** - ESLint configuration
- **[.prettierrc](mdc:.prettierrc)** - Prettier formatting rules

## Choosing the Right Package

- **Universal logic** → `packages/universal`
- **Browser-specific code** → `packages/browser` 
- **Node.js server code** → `packages/node`
- **React components** → `packages/next-react`
- **Type definitions** → `packages/types`

## Testing

Each package has its own `__tests__` directory. Tests use Vitest and follow the pattern:
- Unit tests: `*.test.ts`
- Component tests: `*.test.tsx` (for React components)
